      "side": 1,
      "message": "This (and the command above) will schedule an update of status to BatteryStats in its own Worker: \n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/BatteryService.java;drc\u003dbe26ce76b76441782ce63b61ce1198192da8ab1b;l\u003d495\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/BatteryStatsService.java;drc\u003d1956f4c7003492f868aa824e09d7fd432866afe0;l\u003d1231\n\nBut \"pretend-screen-off\" or \"--reset\" below seem to be applied outside of that Worker; so it may be done before or after \"unplug\" or \"set status\" are applied I think. This could be a source of flakes.\n\nTo be safe, I think it would be better to make sure the batterystats are synced (the worker is done processing) before calling pretend-screen-off. I think this can be done with: dumpsys batterystats --write:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/BatteryStatsService.java;drc\u003d1956f4c7003492f868aa824e09d7fd432866afe0;l\u003d1469\n\nAs it calls \"syncStats\" which will wait for the Worker to finish the task before continuing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 31
      },
